--------------------------------------------------------------------------
What was inherited from mixpanel-react-native
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The package structure and integration approach are adapted from
mixpanel-react-native 3.6.0. Specifically:

  Repository layout
      The src/ + ios/ + android/ split, the podspec reading its version from
      package.json, and the react-native.config.js autolinking declaration.

  Bridging approach
      One promise per native method, a single native module class per
      platform, and a typed declaration file as the public contract.

  Test structure
      The jest layout under __tests__/, and the practice of asserting on the
      arguments handed to the native module rather than on native behaviour.

No Mixpanel source code is copied verbatim into this repository. Every file
here is written against Intempt's own SDK API contract
(intempt-swift/docs/SDK-API-CONTRACT.md).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
What was deliberately NOT inherited
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  JS-mode feature flags
      mixpanel-react-native evaluates feature flags in JavaScript
      (javascript/mixpanel-flags*.js, ~1,700 lines). Intempt has no
      equivalent product surface.

  JavaScript queue, network and persistence layers
      Both Intempt native SDKs own queueing, retry and durable storage. A
      second queue in JavaScript would be a worse one.

  People / super-properties / group-profile APIs
      Not part of Intempt's data model.
